//! Caller-code migration.
//!
//! Generated-setter call sites are rewritten only when the call is proved to
//! reach the generated method: its receiver is proved, by declaration
//! identity, to be a type generated by an `api!` declaration of the same
//! crate (typed bindings, fields, function results, UFCS prefixes and
//! constructor paths are resolved through the crate's modules, items, imports
//! and generic parameters, see [`super::resolve`], never from a last path
//! segment or a member name alone), and method resolution provably selects
//! the generated inherent method:
//!
//! * a standard wrapper or reference of a generated type is not that type;
//!   only an explicit `?`, `unwrap()`, `expect(..)` or `*` looks through it,
//!   and auto-deref reaches the generated method only where Rust allows it (a
//!   `self` method through a `Box`, a `&self` method through any reference or
//!   smart pointer) and no trait implemented in the crate may be selected at
//!   an earlier probe step;
//! * a method chain advances only through methods the generated surface
//!   defines, with their known result types;
//! * names a pattern macro or an unproved statement macro may bind are
//!   unknown.
//!
//! Receivers that are not proved produce precise diagnostics instead of a
//! rename. References to the v2.1 crate-level `ClientBuilder` move into the
//! generated support module (`client::ClientBuilder`) when proved.

